WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:05.609
Speaker 1: One of the narratives that's been
built up by the right wing during the Biden

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:08.480
presidency, and in particular, they were they
were building this up during the lead up to

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:13.980
last week's Biden Putin summit was the Joe
Biden dimentia narrative.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.980
It's not a new narrative.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:21.089
Remember that back when the twenty twenty
Democratic primary was going on, when it got

00:00:21.089 --> 00:00:27.759
down to just Joe Biden versus Bernie Sanders,
many right wingers and even some people on

00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:31.970
the left were saying this is when Biden falls
apart.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:37.260
This is when in a one on one debate against
Bernie Sanders, Joe Biden becomes completely

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.020
unable to put together a single coherent sentence.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.530
And it just didn't happen, as we know.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.710
But they've continued to push this narrative
during the Biden presidency.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.770
Sometimes it's saying, you know, it's really
Kamala Harris who's running the show.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.770
Biden can't do anything.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:55.440
He's just you know, he's an empty suit and
someone else is controlling him.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.780
Sometimes it's saying Biden can't do anything
without notes.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.540
Imagine, right.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.820
Being prepared for meetings.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.120
That's what I call it.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.770
And every single one of these claims that
now is when it'll really become clear.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:13.930
Biden can't even he doesn't even know what
day it is every single time it fails to materialize.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.460
But they were pushing it again for the Biden
Putin summit.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.870
It didn't happen, but it also didn't happen.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:26.280
And it didn't matter that it didn't happen
because in the aftermath, they were still

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.750
saying, whoa, did you see Biden really concerning
behavior?

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.240
And here is Ronnie Jackson.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.260
This was Donald Trump's White House doctor
for a while now.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:41.090
A Congressman, Ronnie Jackson, went on Fox
News and said, from what I'm seeing, Joe Biden

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:47.120
really needs a cognitive test, that Montreal
cognitive assessment that Trump took.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.810
And then Ronnie says, remember, Trump got
a perfect score on that test and then walks

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.720
that back and says, well, he did really well.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.350
Speaker 3: It was submitted to that.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.880
President Trump, as you mentioned, he did
he had a perfect score on his cognitive tests

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.300
and outstanding performance.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.049
And I'm just saying now I'm saying that is
the new standard the president has been set.

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:08.149
And I'm asking Joe Biden and his medical team
to get out there and to get this physical

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:12.260
exam done, get this cognitive testing done
and get the results back to the American people.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.180
We need to know that we can trust our president.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:18.459
Speaker 1: Now, there is just so much here
to talk about.

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:22.900
First of all, notice that Ronnie Jackson first
says Trump got a perfect score.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.480
Then he walked it back and said, well, it
was an outstanding performance.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.020
What he's referring to is when Donald Trump
took that Montreal cognitive assessment, which

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.650
is really meant to screen out serious dementia,
it's like, what city are you in?

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:43.050
Can you identify whether a drawing is a lizard
or a tiger? Trump didn't get a perfect score,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:47.200
but even if Trump did get a perfect score,
it wouldn't tell us that much.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:53.020
You're really supposed to get a near perfect
score unless you're seriously cognitively

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.020
struggling.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:58.580
You give that test to people you suspect have
pretty serious dementia or they've suffered

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.680
a stroke and you want to evaluate how they're
doing cognitively at a high level or maybe

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.150
there's been a brain injury, et cetera.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:10.500
The idea that Trump's near perfect score on
that test is now a baseline for evaluating

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.660
Joe Biden.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:16.910
It's it's all a backwards series of events
saying Trump score was great on that.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:21.380
So Biden should take it is like saying I got
a really good score on a drug test.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.510
Well, it's like, no, you just weren't using
drugs.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.900
There was the absence of a drug problem.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:32.110
The test is meant to screen out the presence
or absence of serious cognitive issues.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:38.230
If the new standard is knowing that a camel
isn't a shark and that, you know, we're in

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.730
Washington, D.C., then we're in real trouble.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:48.690
And then for a doctor to go on TV and say
this bare bones test to rule out severe dementia

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.870
is now the standard for the presidency.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:52.959
That's scary as well.

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:55.680
Now, let's get back to the Biden dementia
stuff.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:01.110
I have been saying without any hesitation
or equivocation since day one of.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:09.510
Joe Biden's 20 20 candidacy, Joe Biden is
not the same Joe Biden as in 2012 when he

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:13.069
debated and ran circles around Paul Ryan.

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:17.450
Joe Biden's speech has slowed down over the
last decade.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.310
Joe Biden is almost 80 years old.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.530
I've conceded that as if it's even really
a concession.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:28.169
I've also talked about how Joe Biden's lifelong
stutter, combined with him being nearly 80

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:33.280
and just talking more slowly now, could make
it seem as though maybe he's not one hundred

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.139
percent clear in his mind all the time.

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:37.040
I have no interest in gaslighting.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.210
It can appear that way when you combine the
slowed down speech with the stutter.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:46.190
But when you see Biden given the opportunity
to lay out his thoughts in a normal setting,

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:51.050
you realize that the guy's memory easily recalls
even small details about conversations that

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:54.919
took place last week and about conversations
that took place last decade.

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:59.440
He has a full understanding of the context
of every issue he's asked about, and I have

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:05.199
no question right now about his ability to
do the job, particularly compared to Donald

00:05:05.199 --> 00:05:06.199
Trump.

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:07.680
Orders of magnitude better now.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.860
Is this the same guy that was Joe Biden debating
Paul Ryan in 2012?

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:13.200
Of course not.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:19.870
And along the same lines, if you look at an
interview, at an interview that now I'm having

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:25.240
the issue at an interview that Trump did with
Dave Letterman 12 years ago, Trump's facility

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:30.130
with words, his vocabulary, his entire way
of speaking, has also shifted dramatically.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:37.169
And one of the things you notice with Trump,
which can be a concerning sign, is his vocabulary

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:44.500
is so limited compared to how he spoke a decade
or two ago in those interviews with Dave Letterman

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.500
and others.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:50.040
Now, if I thought Joe Biden was having a real
cognitive issue, I would just tell you I have

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:55.660
no more interest in having a president with
a cognitive issue than I guess any Republican

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:59.990
does, although they seemed not as worried
about it when Trump couldn't identify that

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:03.980
Rudy Giuliani was across the table from them
or couldn't identify that his limo was right

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:06.979
in front of him when he got off Air Force
One and walked down and had to be brought

00:06:06.979 --> 00:06:12.169
back by Secret Service, or when he said he
wanted to get to the orange is of an investigation.

00:06:12.169 --> 00:06:16.860
The same people now concerned about Biden
weren't concerned then.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.290
I've called it like I've seen it all along.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:25.140
But to hear this from Ronnie Jackson, the
guy doesn't even have experience selecting

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.710
and conducting these types of tests.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:32.570
He's the guy who told us Trump is six foot
three and weighs to thirty nine, if you can

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.199
believe that.

00:06:34.199 --> 00:06:39.350
And even people with mild dementia can actually
pass the Montreal cognitive assessment.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:41.620
So that's the latest from Ronay.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.680
They're continuing to push this same thing.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.760
And I'm curious to hear from you what you
make of it.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.090
Are they pushing this because they have nothing
else?

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:54.800
Are they pushing it to sort of sort of try
to get back at the concerns about the same

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.100
with Donald Trump?

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.100
I don't know.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.139
Let me know what you think.

00:06:58.139 --> 00:07:02.809
We'll have more on this on the show's Instagram,
which you can find at David Pakman show

